1378 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The rate of unemployment - when labour is scarce, either locally or nationally, and there are perceived shortages of skilled workers, then the balance of power tilts towards unions. Competitive pressures in product markets - when a firm is enjoying a dominant monopoly position and high levels of supernormal profit, the unions will know that the employer has the financial resources to meet a more generous wage settlement. When demand for a product is price inelastic, so the demand for labour will tend to be relatively inelastic, this gives the union the opportunity to boost the total)
/E (The rate of unemployment - when labour is scarce, either locally or nationally, and there are perceived shortages of skilled workers, then the balance of power tilts towards unions. Competitive pressures in product markets - when a firm is enjoying a dominant monopoly position and high levels of supernormal profit, the unions will know that the employer has the financial resources to meet a more generous wage settlement. When demand for a product is price inelastic, so the demand for labour will tend to be relatively inelastic, this gives the union the opportunity to boost the total)
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [7]
>>
